patch_description:
This approach performs an offline portfolio search instead of committing to one destination heuristic. It simulates many complete valid solutions using different destination priorities, then outputs the lowest-energy plan found.

Each simulated policy selects a destination by balancing:
- a high minimum remaining label in the destination stack, so boxes needed soon are not buried;
- low destination height, reducing future obstruction;
- optional preference for a high top label;
- deterministic small diversification noise to explore structurally different plans.

Because there are only 200 boxes and 10 stacks, hundreds of full simulations are inexpensive. The best complete simulated plan is retained, guaranteeing legality while usually finding a lower-energy arrangement than a single fixed greedy rule.
